    "title": "A $2$-group criterion in $S_6$",
    "full_tex": "Let $a,b,c\\in\\Sp(4,2)\\cong S_6$. If $\\langle a,cb^{-1}\\rangle$, $\\langle b,ca^{-1}\\rangle$ and $\\langle c,ba^{-1}\\rangle$ are $2$-groups, then so is $\\langle a,b,c\\rangle$.\n"
